KEY FEATURES OF GST
The salient features of GST are as under:
The territorial spread of GST in whole country.
GST is applicable on the supply of goods or services.
it is based on the principle of destination-based
consumption tax against the present principles of originbased taxation.
Import of goods and services is treated as interstate
supplies and would be subject to IGST in addition to the
applicable customs duties.
CGST (Central GST), SGST (State GST) and IGST (Interstate
GST) are levied at rates mutually agreed upon by the centre
and states under the guidance of GST council.
There are four tax slabs namely 5 per cent, 12 per cent, 18 per
cent and 28 per cent for all goods or services.
There is no tax on export and supplies to SEZ.
